{"type":"standard","title":"Derek Tran","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Derek Tran</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q131339671","titles":{"canonical":"Derek_Tran","normalized":"Derek Tran","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Derek Tran</span></span>"},"pageid":78340673,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Rep._Derek_Tran_Official_Portrait.jpg/330px-Rep._Derek_Tran_Official_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/95/Rep._Derek_Tran_Official_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1000,"height":1250},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376436017","tid":"8eaa5398-b7ca-11f1-b37f-eaeae50d275c","timestamp":"2026-09-24T03:46:43Z","description":"American lawyer and politician (born 1980)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derek_Tran","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derek_Tran?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derek_Tran?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Derek_Tran"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derek_Tran","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Derek_Tran","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derek_Tran?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Derek_Tran"}},"extract":"Derek Truyen Tran is an American lawyer and politician who has served as the U.S. representative from California's 45th congressional district since 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, Tran is the third Vietnamese American to be elected to Congress and the first to represent California.","extract_html":"<p><b>Derek Truyen Tran</b> is an American lawyer and politician who has served as the U.S. representative from California's 45th congressional district since 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, Tran is the third Vietnamese American to be elected to Congress and the first to represent California.</p>"}